{"chunk_id": "b4b149eae366", "text": "Bharata, learning that his mother Kaikeyi\u2019s demands led to King Dasharatha\u2019s death and Rama\u2019s exile, erupts in fierce condemnation. He calls her cruel, accuses her of destroying the royal dynasty, and declares that the kingdom she secured for him has only brought him shame. Bharata insists Rama is beloved by all and vows loyalty to his elder brother rather than accepting the throne. To illustrate a mother\u2019s grief, he recounts the story of the divine cow Kamadhenu, who wept on seeing two of her sons suffering under the plough, a scene even Indra witnesses with concern. The tale underscores the depth of maternal love and the cruelty of separating Rama from Kaushalya. Bharata ultimately vows to perform his father\u2019s rites, restore Rama to Ayodhya, and live in the forest himself if necessary.\nBharata angrily condemns Kaikeyi for causing Dasharatha\u2019s death and Rama\u2019s exile, vows loyalty to Rama, and resolves to bring him back and serve him.\nThemes: filial grief, righteous anger, maternal betrayal, devotion to Rama, dharma and kingship", "vector": [0.004228850360959768, -0.02320888638496399, -0.016769349575042725, -0.009400395676493645, -0.0032413441222161055, 0.00019553038873709738, -0.02610335871577263, -0.003402332542464137, -0.028333961963653564, -0.023992253467440605, 0.016331195831298828, 0.007355676963925362, -0.004574062768369913, 0.011584527790546417, -0.013914709910750389, 0.014405974186956882, 0.03640661761164665, 0.0007315014954656363, 0.04431994631886482, -0.015879765152931213, -0.006890968419611454, -0.0010206997394561768, -0.006290166173130274, 0.013728827238082886, -0.01776515506207943, 0.0011410261504352093, 0.020606517791748047, -0.04522280767560005, 0.02169526368379593, -0.02291678451001644, -0.01166419219225645, -0.008391314186155796, 0.012653357349336147, 0.0014820892829447985, -0.030272461473941803, 0.022266192361712456, -0.0022040477488189936, 0.0029658381827175617, 0.01258697